It sounds like a crumbling Victorian conservatory sliding down an Alp, scored by a 22-piece progressive rock orchestra tuned to the biological hum of the earth. Intricate, polyrhythmic time signatures dissolve into sweeping, cinematic Mellotron movements, all while a battered, copper-geared music box plays an unhinged, hypnotic lullaby at the center of the hurricane. The sheer weight of 1970s symphonic art rock is rendered weightless by pristine 432Hz tuning, creating a dense, labyrinthine soundworld that feels simultaneously ancient and radically futuristic.

